{"id": "85938", "name": "חוקי חזקות – כפל חזקות y^a · y^b (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Given that the product \\(y^{{CT:0}} \\cdot y^{{CT:1}} = y^n\\) then</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(n=\\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><p style=\"font-size:0.92em;margin:8px 0 0\">Enter your answer as an integer (whole number) with no decimal point.</p></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Multiplying powers with the same base</b><br>Remember the standard laws of indices: \\(y^{m}\\cdot y^{k}=y^{m+k}\\) (add the exponents).<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ y^{{CT:0}} \\cdot y^{{CT:1}}=y^{{{CT:0}}+{{CT:1}}}=y^{{CT:2}}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "+", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "NumAbsolute", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "n", "testoptions": "0", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "NUM-IND-TRUE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "NUM-IND-0-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "NumAbsolute", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "aval*bval", "testoptions": "0", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "A_TIMES_B", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p>Note that it is not the case in general that \\(y^{a} \\cdot y^{b} = y^{{CT:3}}\\). In fact \\(y^{{CT:3}} = \\left(y^{a}\\right)^{b} = \\left(y^{b}\\right)^{a}\\).</p><p>You may find the identity \\(y^{a} \\times y^{b} = y^{a + b}\\) helpful in solving this problem.</p></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "NUM-IND-1-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["aval", "bval", "n", "ya", "yb"], "nvariants": 9}